From: Fernando Fernandez Mancera <ffmancera@suse.de>
Subject: net/sched: fix pedit partial COW leading to page cache
Patch-mainline: Never, simplified backport of official patch
References: bsc#1265421 CVE-2026-46331

tcf_pedit_act() computes the COW range for skb_ensure_writable()
once before the key loop using tcfp_off_max_hint, but the hint does
not account for the runtime header offset added by typed keys. This
can leave part of the write region un-COW'd.

Fix by linearizing skbs with shared frags upfront to prevent silent data
corruption when pedit operates on ZC pages.

Signed-off-by: Fernando Fernandez Mancera <fmancera@suse.de>
Signed-off-by: Steffen Jaeckel <sjaeckel@suse.de>
---
 net/sched/act_pedit.c |    6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/net/sched/act_pedit.c
+++ b/net/sched/act_pedit.c
@@ -140,6 +140,12 @@ static int tcf_pedit(struct sk_buff *skb
 	if (p->tcfp_nkeys > 0) {
 		struct tc_pedit_key *tkey = p->tcfp_keys;
 
+		/* Linearize so we are sure pedit is operating on a private copy */
+		if (skb_shinfo(skb)->nr_frags > 0) {
+			if (__skb_linearize(skb))
+				goto bad;
+		}
+
 		for (i = p->tcfp_nkeys; i > 0; i--, tkey++) {
 			u32 *ptr, _data;
 			int offset = tkey->off;
